configuration.analysisConfiguration:
{
  "revapi": {
    "semver": {
      "ignore": {
        "enabled": true,
        "versionIncreaseAllows": {
          "major": "breaking",
          "minor": "nonBreaking",
          "patch": "equivalent"
        }
      }
    },
    "differences": {
      "ignore": true,
      "differences": [
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.missing\\.(new|old)Class",
          "justification": "A TYPE THAT IS ABSENT FROM BOTH ARCHIVES, NOT A DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THEM, and the narrower half of this problem was fixed at its cause rather than listed here. Two kinds of missing class showed up on the first gated build. The first was jakarta.servlet.HttpServletRequest and friends in odata-filter: resolvable, just not resolved, because they arrive transitively at `provided` scope - that is fixed above with resolveTransitiveProvidedDependencies, and it is fixed there and not here on purpose, because ignoring a class revapi COULD have loaded turns an incorrect analysis into a quiet one. The second kind cannot be fixed that way: spring-security-config's HttpSecurity declares saml2Login(), ldapAuthentication() and oauth2Client(), whose types live in spring-security-saml2-service-provider, spring-security-ldap and spring-security-oauth2-client - jars this platform does not depend on and should not start depending on to satisfy a checker. Twenty-three of them, reachable only through Spring's own types, which the design-advisory exemption below already covers. They are absent from the old archive and the new one alike, so they can never constitute a difference between two releases; what they would do armed is fail every build forever. If a type of OURS ever goes missing that is java.class.removed, which stays armed."
        },
        {
          "code": "java.class.removed",
          "old": "class ru.ludwigandreas.pat.web.PatCredentialNotPermittedException",
          "justification": "REMOVED FROM pat-spring-boot-starter IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION - change admin-authorization. The type moved, unchanged in behaviour and keeping its problem code ludwig.pat.credential-not-permitted, to security-spring-boot-starter as ru.ludwigandreas.security.web.PatCredentialNotPermittedException, because the administrative surface guard there must refuse a PAT credential with the very same problem type as the PAT management surface, and pat-spring-boot-starter depends on the security starter rather than the other way round. Migration: change the import."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.addedToInterface",
          "new": "method long ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.pat\\.repository\\.PatQueryRepository::recordUse\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "ADDED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change gate-hygiene. The last-use write became a version-less update so that a revoke or rotation overlapping a token's use no longer fails with an optimistic-lock conflict. A custom PatQueryRepository implementation must add recordUse(id, usedAt, sourceIp): update last_used_at, last_used_ip and use_count + 1 for the id, only when the stored last use is null or earlier, without touching the version."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.parameterTypeChanged",
          "old": "parameter void ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.pat\\.service\\.PatUsageTracker::<init>\\(===ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.pat\\.repository\\.PatRepository===,.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change gate-hygiene. PatUsageTracker used PatRepository only for the read-modify-save last-use write that raced revocation; it now takes PatQueryRepository and calls its version-less recordUse. Migration: pass the PatQueryRepository bean instead of PatRepository."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.numberOfParametersChanged",
          "old": "method void ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.security\\.admin\\.AdminHandlerValidator::<init>\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change admin-surface-polish. AdminHandlerValidator now also fails startup when a catalogued administrative operation's description key resolves in no bundle, so it takes the ProblemMessages it resolves them through as a third constructor argument. Migration: pass the ProblemMessages bean; a service using AdminAutoConfiguration is unaffected."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.addedToInterface",
          "new": "method long ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.fileaction\\.repository\\.FileActionSubmissionQueryRepository::(cancelIfValidated|startIfValidated)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "ADDED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change file-action-cancelled-state. A cancel and a confirm racing on one VALIDATED submission are now two conditional updates on the same predicate, so exactly one wins. The interface is the module's own query fragment, implemented by FileActionSubmissionQueryRepositoryImpl; a custom implementation must add both, each a version-bumping update WHERE state = 'VALIDATED' that refreshes the copy the persistence context holds."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(addedToInterface|defaultMethodAddedToInterface)",
          "new": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.outbox\\.(repository\\.OutboxMessageRepositoryCustom::purgeFinishedBefore|metrics\\.OutboxMetrics::recordPurged)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "ADDED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change outbox-retention-purge. The outbox purges terminal messages after their retention period. OutboxMessageRepositoryCustom is the module's own repository fragment, implemented by OutboxMessageRepositoryCustomImpl; a custom implementation must add purgeFinishedBefore(status, cutoff, limit), a bounded SKIP LOCKED delete of messages and their history in one transaction. OutboxMetrics.recordPurged is a default method, so existing implementations keep compiling and simply do not count purges."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(removed|numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged|returnTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.reconciliation\\.(engine\\.TaskRunner::(dryRun|backfill|<init>)|admin\\.service\\.ReconciliationAdminService::(run|backfill)|admin\\.service\\.ReconciliationAdminService\\.Engine::<init>)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "REMOVED OR CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION - change reconciliation-run-history. Operator-triggered runs became recorded, asynchronous runs: TaskRunner.dryRun and backfill (synchronous, unrecorded) are replaced by start(task, tier, kind, keys, triggeredBy), and the runner takes a RunRecorder and the manual-run executor; the admin service's run/backfill return the run record; Engine gains the run repository. Migration: call TaskRunner.start and poll the run, or use the administrative endpoints."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(addedToInterface|defaultMethodAddedToInterface)",
          "new": "method void ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.reconciliation\\.metrics\\.ReconciliationMetrics::recordRunRecordFailed\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "ADDED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change reconciliation-run-history. A default method, so an implementation written before run history keeps compiling and simply does not count failed history writes."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(removed|numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged|returnTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.messaging\\.db\\.admin\\.(service\\.MessagingAdminService::(<init>|consumers)|web\\.MessagingAdminController::consumers)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "REMOVED OR CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION - change messaging-db-consumer-controls. The messaging admin area can pause, resume and move a database-log consumer: the service takes the service's local consumer groups and AdminAudit besides the LogStore, and consumers() returns ConsumerView (the position fields plus paused, pausedBy, pausedAt) - the JSON listing only gains fields. Migration: let the auto-configuration build the service, or pass the group supplier and AdminAudit."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method void ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.audit\\.Actor::<init>\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION - change admin-delegation-claim. Actor gains via, the party the request came through (RFC 8693 act.sub), as its last component, so that it is stored and searchable rather than an attribute. The factories Actor.of and Actor.system keep their signatures and record no via. Migration: append null (or the acting party) to a canonical-constructor call."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.audit\\.store\\.(repository\\.AuditTrailQuery::<init>|admin\\.service\\.AuditTrailSearch\\.(Filter|EventView)::<init>|admin\\.web\\.AuditTrailController::events)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION - change admin-delegation-claim. The audit trail can be searched by acting party: AuditTrailQuery and the search Filter gain via, EventView shows it, and GET /admin/v1/audit/events gains an optional via parameter. Migration: build AuditTrailQuery with its builder (unchanged), and add via (or null) to a positional Filter or EventView construction."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.messaging\\.db\\.config\\.MessagingDbAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigMessagingAdminService\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change messaging-db-consumer-controls (recorded late, during admin-object-scope). The bean method takes the listener registry and AdminAudit for the service's new constructor. Auto-configuration bean methods are called by Spring, not by consumers; a service that declares its own MessagingAdminService bean is unaffected."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.(security\\.config\\.(AdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigAdminAccessEvaluator|DataAuthorizationAutoConfiguration::ludwigDataScopePolicyValidator)|reconciliation\\.config\\.ReconciliationAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigReconciliationAdminService)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change admin-object-scope. Administrative operations can be scoped to named objects: the evaluator and the reconciliation admin service take the AdminObjectScope, and the policy validator the administrative areas it checks admin.* policies against. Auto-configuration bean methods are called by Spring, not by consumers; the types' previous constructors are kept."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.security\\.config\\.AdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigAdminSurfaceGuard\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change admin-four-eyes-approval. The surface guard holds calls whose operation requires approval, so its bean method takes AdminApprovals. Auto-configuration bean methods are called by Spring, not by consumers; AdminSurfaceGuard keeps its previous constructors."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.(removed|numberOfParametersChanged|parameterTypeChanged)",
          "old": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.(audit\\.store\\.(admin\\.(service\\.AuditTrailSearch::(<init>|search)|web\\.AuditTrailController::events)|repository\\.AuditEventQueryRepository(Impl)?::findPage|repository\\.AuditTrailQuery::<init>|config\\.AuditAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigAuditTrailSearch)|outbox\\.(admin\\.(service\\.OutboxAdminService::(<init>|messages)|web\\.OutboxAdminController::messages)|repository\\.OutboxAdminQueries::page|config\\.OutboxAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigOutboxAdminService)|reconciliation\\.(admin\\.(service\\.ReconciliationAdminService::(<init>|runs)|web\\.ReconciliationAdminController::runs)|config\\.ReconciliationAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigReconciliationAdminService)|export\\.(admin\\.(service\\.ExportAdminService::(<init>|runs)|web\\.ExportAdminController::runs)|repository\\.ExportAdminQueries::runs|config\\.ExportAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigExportAdminService)|fileaction\\.(admin\\.(service\\.FileActionAdminService::(<init>|submissions)|web\\.FileActionAdminController::submissions)|repository\\.FileActionAdminQueries::submissions|config\\.FileActionAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigFileActionAdminService)|pat\\.(admin\\.(service\\.PatAdminService::(<init>|tokens)|web\\.PatAdminController::tokens)|repository\\.PatQueryRepository(Impl)?::findForAdministration|autoconfigure\\.PatAdminAutoConfiguration::ludwigPatAdminService)|odatafilter\\.core\\.ODataQuery::<init>)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "REMOVED OR CHANGED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION (no backward compatibility) - change admin-listing-odata-filter. The six paged administrative listings filter with OData $filter only: their explicit filter parameters are removed, and the services, repository methods and auto-configuration bean methods take the parsed predicate or db-core's AdminQueryFilter instead. ODataQuery's constructor carries the FilterSummary. AuditTrailQuery loses via. Migration: send $filter (e.g. ?status=FAILED becomes $filter=status eq 'FAILED'); build the services through their auto-configuration."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.class\\.removed",
          "old": "(enum|class) ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.(pat\\.admin\\.service\\.PatAdminService\\.TokenStatus|audit\\.store\\.admin\\.service\\.AuditTrailSearch\\.Filter)",
          "justification": "REMOVED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE WITHOUT A PRIOR DEPRECATION, BY THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT DECISION - change admin-listing-odata-filter. The PAT listing's status enum and the audit search's Filter record were the removed parameters' types. Migration: filter on revokedAt/expiresAt, and on the audit event's fields, with $filter."
        },
        {
          "regex": true,
          "code": "java\\.method\\.addedToInterface",
          "new": "method .* ru\\.ludwigandreas\\.cache\\.api\\.LudwigCacheRegistry::(evictAll|settings)\\(.*\\)",
          "justification": "ADDED IN THE NEXT MAJOR RELEASE, change replica-control-broadcast. The registry clears one cache by name (local and shared tier) and lists every cache's resolved settings, for job-core's caches area and its cacheevict replica control. DefaultLudwigCacheRegistry implements both; a custom registry must add them."
        },
        {
